{"task_id": "Mbpp/9", "solution": "def find_Rotations(s: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the minimum number of rotations (greater than 0) required to get the same string.\n    Raises TypeError for invalid input (None, non-string, or empty string).\n    \"\"\"\n    # Input validation as per design context\n    if not isinstance(s, str) or s is None:\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be a string.\")\n    if not s: # Handles empty string, considered invalid length 0 as per design\n        raise TypeError(\"Input string cannot be empty.\")\n\n    n = len(s)\n\n    # Iterate through possible positive rotation counts k, from 1 up to n-1.\n    # The design specifies returning len(s) if no smaller k exists.\n    for k in range(1, n):\n        # Perform a left-rotation as defined in the design: s[k:] + s[:k]\n        rotated_s = s[k:] + s[:k]\n        if rotated_s == s:\n            return k\n    \n    # If the loop completes, it means no rotation k (where 1 <= k < n) resulted in the original string.\n    # In this case, n rotations are required to return to the original string.\n    return n"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/12", "solution": "def _row_sum(row: list[float]) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Computes the arithmetic sum of numeric elements in a row.\"\"\"\n    return sum(row)\n\ndef validate_matrix(matrix: object) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Validates that the input is a list of lists containing only numeric elements.\"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(matrix, list):\n        raise ValueError(\"Input matrix must be a list.\")\n    if not matrix: # Allow empty matrix\n        return\n\n    for i, row in enumerate(matrix):\n        if not isinstance(row, list):\n            raise ValueError(f\"Row at index {i} must be a list.\")\n        for j, element in enumerate(row):\n            if not isinstance(element, (int, float)):\n                raise ValueError(f\"Element at [{i}][{j}] must be numeric (int or float).\")\n\ndef sort_matrix(matrix: list[list[float]]) -> list[list[float]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sorts a matrix in ascending order based on the sum of its rows.\n    Validates input and uses a stable sort.\n    \"\"\"\n    validate_matrix(matrix)\n\n    rows_with_sums = [(row, _row_sum(row)) for row in matrix]\n    rows_with_sums.sort(key=lambda item: item[1])\n\n    return [row for (row, s) in rows_with_sums]"}
