{"task_id": "Mbpp/14", "solution": "class TriangularPrism:\n    \"\"\"Represents the dimensions of a triangular prism.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, base: float, height: float, length: float) -> None:\n        self.base = base\n        self.height = height\n        self.length = length\n\nclass InputValidator:\n    \"\"\"Validates if a given value is numeric (int or float).\"\"\"\n    def isNumeric(self, value) -> bool:\n        return isinstance(value, (int, float))\n\nclass VolumeCalculator:\n    \"\"\"Orchestrates validation and computation of triangular prism volume.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, validator: InputValidator = None) -> None:\n        self._validator = validator if validator is not None else InputValidator()\n\n    def computeVolume(self, prism: TriangularPrism) -> float:\n        \"\"\"Calculates the volume of a triangular prism.\"\"\"\n        return 0.5 * prism.base * prism.height * prism.length\n\n    def find_Volume(self, base, height, length) -> float:\n        \"\"\"Validates inputs, constructs a prism, and computes its volume.\"\"\"\n        if not (self._validator.isNumeric(base) and\n                self._validator.isNumeric(height) and\n                self._validator.isNumeric(length)):\n            raise TypeError(\"base, height and length must be numeric\")\n        \n        prism = TriangularPrism(float(base), float(height), float(length))\n        return self.computeVolume(prism)\n\ndef find_Volume(base, height, length) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the volume of a triangular prism.\n    Delegates to an internal VolumeCalculator for computation and validation.\n    \"\"\"\n    calculator = VolumeCalculator()\n    return calculator.find_Volume(base, height, length)"}
