{"task_id": "Mbpp/71", "solution": "from typing import List\n\ndef comb_sort(input_list: List) -> List:\n    \"\"\"Sorts a list of elements in ascending order using the Comb Sort algorithm.\n    It returns a new sorted list, preserving the original.\"\"\"\n    n = len(input_list)\n    if n == 0:\n        return []\n\n    arr = list(input_list)  # Create a mutable copy to avoid modifying the original list\n    gap = n\n    shrink_factor = 1.3\n    swapped = True\n\n    while gap > 1 or swapped:\n        gap = int(gap / shrink_factor)\n        if gap < 1:\n            gap = 1\n\n        swapped = False\n        for i in range(n - gap):\n            if arr[i] > arr[i + gap]:\n                arr[i], arr[i + gap] = arr[i + gap], arr[i]\n                swapped = True\n    return arr"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/74", "solution": "def is_samepatterns(list_a, list_b):\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if list_a follows the sequence pattern defined by list_b.\n    Ensures a consistent and injective (one-to-one) mapping between elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(list_a) != len(list_b):\n        return False\n\n    # mapping_a_to_b stores the mapping from elements of list_a to elements of list_b.\n    mapping_a_to_b = {}\n    # mapping_b_to_a stores the reverse mapping, ensuring injectivity.\n    mapping_b_to_a = {}\n\n    for i in range(len(list_a)):\n        char_a = list_a[i]\n        char_b = list_b[i]\n\n        # Check consistency for char_a:\n        # If char_a has been mapped before, ensure it maps to the same char_b.\n        if char_a in mapping_a_to_b:\n            if mapping_a_to_b[char_a] != char_b:\n                return False\n        else:\n            # If char_a is new, add its mapping.\n            mapping_a_to_b[char_a] = char_b\n\n        # Check injectivity for char_b:\n        # If char_b has been mapped before, ensure it maps from the same char_a.\n        # This prevents different char_a's from mapping to the same char_b.\n        if char_b in mapping_b_to_a:\n            if mapping_b_to_a[char_b] != char_a:\n                return False\n        else:\n            # If char_b is new, add its reverse mapping.\n            mapping_b_to_a[char_b] = char_a\n\n    return True"}
