{"task_id": "Mbpp/84", "solution": "class SequenceError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Custom exception for Newman-Conway sequence related errors.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str):\n        super().__init__(message)\n\nclass InputValidator:\n    \"\"\"Validates input 'n' for the Newman-Conway sequence.\"\"\"\n    def validate(self, n) -> None:\n        if not isinstance(n, int):\n            raise SequenceError(\"Input 'n' must be an integer.\")\n        if n < 1:\n            raise SequenceError(\"Input 'n' must be a positive integer (n >= 1).\")\n\nclass NewmanConwaySequence:\n    \"\"\"Computes and memoizes values for the Newman-Conway sequence.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self):\n        self._cache: dict[int, int] = {}\n        self._initialized: bool = False\n\n    def init(self) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Initializes the cache with base cases a(1)=1 and a(2)=1.\"\"\"\n        if not self._initialized:\n            self._cache[1] = 1\n            self._cache[2] = 1\n            self._initialized = True\n\n    def compute(self, n: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Calculates the nth Newman-Conway number using memoization.\"\"\"\n        if n in self._cache:\n            return self._cache[n]\n\n        # Base cases (already covered by init, but can serve as a fallback or for direct compute calls)\n        if n == 1 or n == 2:\n            self._cache[n] = 1\n            return 1\n\n        # Recursive step: a(n) = a(a(n-1)) + a(n - a(n-1))\n        an_minus_1 = self.compute(n - 1)\n        value = self.compute(an_minus_1) + self.compute(n - an_minus_1)\n        \n        self._cache[n] = value\n        return value\n\n_calculator: NewmanConwaySequence = NewmanConwaySequence()\n_validator: InputValidator = InputValidator()\n\ndef sequence(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the nth number in the Newman-Conway sequence.\n    Validates input and computes the sequence value using memoization.\n    \"\"\"\n    _validator.validate(n)\n    _calculator.init()\n    return _calculator.compute(n)"}
