{"task_id": "Mbpp/223", "solution": "def _first_index(arr, effective_n, x):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the first occurrence of x in arr[0:effective_n] using binary search.\n    Returns its index or -1 if not found.\n    \"\"\"\n    low = 0\n    high = effective_n - 1\n    result = -1\n\n    while low <= high:\n        mid = (low + high) // 2\n        if arr[mid] == x:\n            result = mid\n            high = mid - 1\n        elif arr[mid] < x:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else:\n            high = mid - 1\n    return result\n\ndef _last_index(arr, effective_n, x):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the last occurrence of x in arr[0:effective_n] using binary search.\n    Returns its index or -1 if not found.\n    \"\"\"\n    low = 0\n    high = effective_n - 1\n    result = -1\n\n    while low <= high:\n        mid = (low + high) // 2\n        if arr[mid] == x:\n            result = mid\n            low = mid + 1\n        elif arr[mid] < x:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else:\n            high = mid - 1\n    return result\n\ndef _count_occurrences(arr, n, x):\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts occurrences of x in the array arr up to index n-1.\n    Uses binary search helpers for efficiency.\n    \"\"\"\n    effective_n = min(len(arr), n)\n\n    if effective_n == 0:\n        return 0\n\n    first = _first_index(arr, effective_n, x)\n    if first == -1:\n        return 0\n\n    last = _last_index(arr, effective_n, x)\n    return last - first + 1\n\ndef is_majority(arr, n, x):\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if an element x is the majority element in a sorted array arr of length n.\n    A majority element occurs more than n/2 times.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return False\n\n    count = _count_occurrences(arr, n, x)\n    return count > n / 2"}
