{"task_id": "Mbpp/283", "solution": "import collections\n\ndef validate(value: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the frequency of each digit in the integer is less than or equal to the digit itself.\n    This function processes the absolute value of the input to extract digits.\n    \"\"\"\n    s_value = str(abs(value))\n    \n    # Calculate the frequency of each digit present in the number.\n    digit_counts = collections.Counter(int(d) for d in s_value)\n\n    # Verify that for each digit, its frequency is less than or equal to the digit's value.\n    for digit, frequency in digit_counts.items():\n        if frequency > digit:\n            return False\n            \n    return True"}
