{"task_id": "Mbpp/391", "solution": "def _is_numeric(value: any) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Return True if value is int or float (numeric); used by _validate_inputs.\"\"\"\n    return isinstance(value, (int, float))\n\ndef _validate_inputs(ids: list, names: list, scores: list) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Raise ValueError/TypeError on invalid inputs: non-list inputs, unequal lengths, or invalid element types.\"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(ids, list):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input 'ids' must be a list.\")\n    if not isinstance(names, list):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input 'names' must be a list.\")\n    if not isinstance(scores, list):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input 'scores' must be a list.\")\n\n    if not (len(ids) == len(names) == len(scores)):\n        raise ValueError(\"All input lists must have the same length.\")\n\n    for i in range(len(ids)):\n        if not isinstance(ids[i], str):\n            raise TypeError(f\"Element at index {i} in 'ids' must be a string.\")\n        if not isinstance(names[i], str):\n            raise TypeError(f\"Element at index {i} in 'names' must be a string.\")\n        if not _is_numeric(scores[i]):\n            raise TypeError(f\"Element at index {i} in 'scores' must be numeric (int or float).\")\n\ndef convert_list_dictionary(ids: list, names: list, scores: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"Validate inputs and return a list of nested dicts where each element i is { ids[i]: { names[i]: scores[i] } }. Raises ValueError or TypeError on invalid inputs.\"\"\"\n    _validate_inputs(ids, names, scores)\n\n    result = []\n    for i in range(len(ids)):\n        result.append({ids[i]: {names[i]: scores[i]}})\n    return result"}
