{"task_id": "Mbpp/406", "solution": "from dataclasses import dataclass\n\n@dataclass\nclass IntegerValue:\n    \"\"\"Represents a single integer input value.\"\"\"\n    value: int\n\n@dataclass\nclass ParityResult:\n    \"\"\"Represents the result of a parity check.\"\"\"\n    is_odd: bool\n\nclass ParityService:\n    \"\"\"\n    A stateless service to determine the parity of an integer.\n    It returns True if the number is odd, False if even.\n    \"\"\"\n    def find_Parity(self, n: int) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"\n        Determines if the given integer is odd.\n        Returns True if odd, False if even.\n        \"\"\"\n        return n % 2 != 0\n\ndef find_Parity(n: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds whether the parity of a given number is odd.\n    Delegates the parity determination to an internal ParityService.\n    \"\"\"\n    service = ParityService()\n    return service.find_Parity(n)"}
