{"task_id": "Mbpp/448", "solution": "class PerrinSequence:\n    def __init__(self):\n        # Stores computed Perrin numbers, initialized with base values P(0), P(1), P(2).\n        self._perrin_numbers = [3, 0, 2]\n\n    def generateUpTo(self, n: int) -> list[int]:\n        # Generates Perrin numbers from P(0) to P(n) using the recurrence relation.\n        # It extends the internal list and returns a slice up to n.\n        if n < 0:\n            return []\n        \n        while len(self._perrin_numbers) <= n:\n            k = len(self._perrin_numbers)\n            # P(k) = P(k-2) + P(k-3) for k > 2\n            next_perrin = self._perrin_numbers[k - 2] + self._perrin_numbers[k - 3]\n            self._perrin_numbers.append(next_perrin)\n            \n        return self._perrin_numbers[:n + 1]\n\n\ndef cal_sum(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of Perrin numbers from P(0) to P(n).\"\"\"\n    perrin_generator = PerrinSequence()\n    perrin_numbers = perrin_generator.generateUpTo(n)\n    return sum(perrin_numbers)"}
